[{:db/id 17592186188280 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-fd7fa324-de44-5c60-a60e-ad08ed2ad90d" "question-673ddc27-8133-50ba-9995-aed461126acc" "question-d216f49f-dbd6-5da5-81b2-ff39a5445339"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188215 :question/problem "A sample $X_1, X_2, \\ldots, X_{8}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu$ and population standard deviation $\\sigma.$ If $\\mu$ and $\\sigma$ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. $\\displaystyle \\min(X_1, X_2, \\dots, X_8)$\n\nII. $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{4} X_{2i}^2$\n\nIII. $\\displaystyle \\sum_{i=1}^{8} \\left( \\dfrac{X_i}{\\sigma} - 1 \\right)^2$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186188279 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-afcca6b7-f927-5420-8ae5-122ee674dc61" "question-e8084345-dfbb-5406-9137-a5e08b474106" "question-d07ab9ad-d8e6-53a3-916d-ef13c3850d54"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186416931 :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{7}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. $({X}_{1}+{X}_{4}+{X}_{7})^{3}$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\frac{({X}_{i}-\\mu )^{2}}{2}$\n\nIII. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{7}\\frac{{X}_{i}^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-fd7fa324-de44-5c60-a60e-ad08ed2ad90d" :question/id #uuid "fd7fa324-de44-5c60-a60e-ad08ed2ad90d" :question/math-academy-id "q-143554" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both  known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}|{X}_{i}-\\mu |$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{12}({X}_{i}+\\sigma )$\n\nIII. $min({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12})$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression.\n\n- Expression I is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12}$ and the *known* population mean $\\mu $ only.\n\n- Expression II is also a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12}$ and the *known* population standard deviation $\\sigma $ only.\n\n- Expression III is also a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{12}$ only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b128b2f5-8e87-5b1c-8970-0c5544ce4df2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b128b2f5-8e87-5b1c-8970-0c5544ce4df2" :answer-field/id #uuid "b128b2f5-8e87-5b1c-8970-0c5544ce4df2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f209a605-cfa0-5945-86f1-b2935fd1a5a0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-471b22b4-5280-5ef4-b6a9-086940207f69" "answer-29453521-97e6-5150-a7bc-602fae176d59" "answer-f209a605-cfa0-5945-86f1-b2935fd1a5a0" "answer-9aee564c-68f0-5f6d-b1c6-b37ef059a00a" "answer-3cdaafcf-a37f-58e8-84d1-3d0c20ba5cfd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-471b22b4-5280-5ef4-b6a9-086940207f69" :answer/id #uuid "471b22b4-5280-5ef4-b6a9-086940207f69" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29453521-97e6-5150-a7bc-602fae176d59" :answer/id #uuid "29453521-97e6-5150-a7bc-602fae176d59" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f209a605-cfa0-5945-86f1-b2935fd1a5a0" :answer/id #uuid "f209a605-cfa0-5945-86f1-b2935fd1a5a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9aee564c-68f0-5f6d-b1c6-b37ef059a00a" :answer/id #uuid "9aee564c-68f0-5f6d-b1c6-b37ef059a00a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cdaafcf-a37f-58e8-84d1-3d0c20ba5cfd" :answer/id #uuid "3cdaafcf-a37f-58e8-84d1-3d0c20ba5cfd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-673ddc27-8133-50ba-9995-aed461126acc" :question/id #uuid "673ddc27-8133-50ba-9995-aed461126acc" :question/math-academy-id "q-143551" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ is unknown and $\\sigma $ is known, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. $max({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{11},\\mu )$\n\nII. $min({X}_{2},{X}_{4},…,{X}_{10},\\sigma )$\n\nIII. $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{11}}{{\\mu }^{2}+{\\sigma }^{2}+1}$" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression.\n\n- Expression I is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\n- Expression II is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{11}$ and the *known* population standard deviation $\\sigma $ only. Note that a statistic doesn't need to include every sample element.\n\n- Expression III is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d8fe19c0-cb1a-5326-b79f-39ab45804633"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d8fe19c0-cb1a-5326-b79f-39ab45804633" :answer-field/id #uuid "d8fe19c0-cb1a-5326-b79f-39ab45804633" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bdd4ce4b-dbef-52fd-bba0-53352940d2eb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-06448ce2-0e18-514f-b68e-1203b53623bf" "answer-5ba67d51-ba43-50e4-9513-6d222e3e8af9" "answer-bdd4ce4b-dbef-52fd-bba0-53352940d2eb" "answer-73623fce-c5b8-5155-ae34-d860b81c911a" "answer-09c7d387-d49f-536a-b195-0974f7eff35f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-06448ce2-0e18-514f-b68e-1203b53623bf" :answer/id #uuid "06448ce2-0e18-514f-b68e-1203b53623bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ba67d51-ba43-50e4-9513-6d222e3e8af9" :answer/id #uuid "5ba67d51-ba43-50e4-9513-6d222e3e8af9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdd4ce4b-dbef-52fd-bba0-53352940d2eb" :answer/id #uuid "bdd4ce4b-dbef-52fd-bba0-53352940d2eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-73623fce-c5b8-5155-ae34-d860b81c911a" :answer/id #uuid "73623fce-c5b8-5155-ae34-d860b81c911a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09c7d387-d49f-536a-b195-0974f7eff35f" :answer/id #uuid "09c7d387-d49f-536a-b195-0974f7eff35f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186416924 :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population standard deviation $\\sigma .$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{15}|{X}_{i}|$\n\nII. $min({X}_{1},{X}_{3},…,{X}_{13},{X}_{15})$\n\nIII. $max({X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{15},\\sigma )$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-d216f49f-dbd6-5da5-81b2-ff39a5445339" :question/id #uuid "d216f49f-dbd6-5da5-81b2-ff39a5445339" :question/math-academy-id "q-139833" :question/problem "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ is drawn from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$ If $\\mu $ and $\\sigma $ are both unknown, which of the following are statistics?\n\nI. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{X}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=6}^{10}{X}_{i}$\n\nII. ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}\\sqrt{{X}_{i}^{2}-{\\sigma }^{2}}$\n\nIII. $\\frac{{X}_{1}+{X}_{10}}{2}+\\mu $" :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each expression. \n\n- Expression I is a statistic. It is a function of the sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{10}$ only.\n\n- Expression II is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population variance ${\\sigma }^{2}.$\n\n- Expression III is *not* a statistic. It is a function that contains the unknown population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f4f0f31-85b3-59bd-8498-64976de6e8b3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f4f0f31-85b3-59bd-8498-64976de6e8b3" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4f0f31-85b3-59bd-8498-64976de6e8b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9e8ef953-c0a1-5782-8534-95a941c3407d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e8ef953-c0a1-5782-8534-95a941c3407d" "answer-2f80261e-f3fc-5e23-8e3f-a6acba9abcf8" "answer-97752404-ed02-56de-92db-254ae5e1b56b" "answer-568b0d55-78f4-5d7c-b63a-bcab6a620e80" "answer-3d10fc58-31b9-561f-8371-ffbba6ce6263"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e8ef953-c0a1-5782-8534-95a941c3407d" :answer/id #uuid "9e8ef953-c0a1-5782-8534-95a941c3407d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2f80261e-f3fc-5e23-8e3f-a6acba9abcf8" :answer/id #uuid "2f80261e-f3fc-5e23-8e3f-a6acba9abcf8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97752404-ed02-56de-92db-254ae5e1b56b" :answer/id #uuid "97752404-ed02-56de-92db-254ae5e1b56b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-568b0d55-78f4-5d7c-b63a-bcab6a620e80" :answer/id #uuid "568b0d55-78f4-5d7c-b63a-bcab6a620e80" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d10fc58-31b9-561f-8371-ffbba6ce6263" :answer/id #uuid "3d10fc58-31b9-561f-8371-ffbba6ce6263" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of those listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-afcca6b7-f927-5420-8ae5-122ee674dc61" :question/id #uuid "afcca6b7-f927-5420-8ae5-122ee674dc61" :question/math-academy-id "q-149835" :question/problem "Suppose the following data are sampled from a population.\n\n$$\n2.3,\\,2.6,\\,3.1,\\,2.8\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the statistic ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{({X}_{i}+1)^{2}}{n-2}$ for this particular sample." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{4}\\frac{({x}_{i}+1)^{2}}{4-2} & =\\frac{1}{2}((2.3+1)^{2}+(2.6+1)^{2}+(3.1+1)^{2}+(2.8+1)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(10.89+12.96+16.81+14.44) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(55.1) \\\\  & =27.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $27.55.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6fd46a11-d062-5fd0-aee5-0dff1aa44f88"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6fd46a11-d062-5fd0-aee5-0dff1aa44f88" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fd46a11-d062-5fd0-aee5-0dff1aa44f88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-05bb2d48-37d8-584c-872b-45fab789e483" :answer-field/choices ["answer-52fdc8a2-4716-5414-bfb3-eb64b770f20c" "answer-23ef56c6-3700-5a51-a7ea-a3fb4bd0dc99" "answer-05bb2d48-37d8-584c-872b-45fab789e483" "answer-be0a8e72-f874-5a97-afaa-e5dd4b41ab6e" "answer-22666824-84aa-5663-9208-faedd927de76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-52fdc8a2-4716-5414-bfb3-eb64b770f20c" :answer/id #uuid "52fdc8a2-4716-5414-bfb3-eb64b770f20c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "21.34" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23ef56c6-3700-5a51-a7ea-a3fb4bd0dc99" :answer/id #uuid "23ef56c6-3700-5a51-a7ea-a3fb4bd0dc99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-05bb2d48-37d8-584c-872b-45fab789e483" :answer/id #uuid "05bb2d48-37d8-584c-872b-45fab789e483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27.55" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be0a8e72-f874-5a97-afaa-e5dd4b41ab6e" :answer/id #uuid "be0a8e72-f874-5a97-afaa-e5dd4b41ab6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-22666824-84aa-5663-9208-faedd927de76" :answer/id #uuid "22666824-84aa-5663-9208-faedd927de76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32.16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8084345-dfbb-5406-9137-a5e08b474106" :question/id #uuid "e8084345-dfbb-5406-9137-a5e08b474106" :question/math-academy-id "q-139837" :question/problem "The weights, in pounds, of six randomly selected newborns drawn from a population were measured. The results are shown below.\n\n$$\n5.5,\\,5.8,\\,6.2,\\,5.1,\\,6.4,\\,6\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the statistic $\\frac{n}{n+1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}$ for this particular sample." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{6+1}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i} & =\\frac{6}{7}(5.5+5.8+6.2+5.1+6.4+6) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{7}(35) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $30\\,\\text{lb}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-98c8d652-8db8-5628-8b26-929615b20791"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-98c8d652-8db8-5628-8b26-929615b20791" :answer-field/id #uuid "98c8d652-8db8-5628-8b26-929615b20791" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0e473785-f50e-53de-86c6-0a0d56d437c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-327520ab-534d-5508-b50a-db2d10472cde" "answer-965e4b74-64fe-591d-9c4c-09d3918cbb1d" "answer-933c8972-9d57-57dd-8bc9-0b6bb925355e" "answer-0e473785-f50e-53de-86c6-0a0d56d437c5" "answer-606a2a26-1a6c-57ef-b3cd-f1e192952714"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-327520ab-534d-5508-b50a-db2d10472cde" :answer/id #uuid "327520ab-534d-5508-b50a-db2d10472cde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28.2\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-965e4b74-64fe-591d-9c4c-09d3918cbb1d" :answer/id #uuid "965e4b74-64fe-591d-9c4c-09d3918cbb1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "29.5\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-933c8972-9d57-57dd-8bc9-0b6bb925355e" :answer/id #uuid "933c8972-9d57-57dd-8bc9-0b6bb925355e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30.4\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0e473785-f50e-53de-86c6-0a0d56d437c5" :answer/id #uuid "0e473785-f50e-53de-86c6-0a0d56d437c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-606a2a26-1a6c-57ef-b3cd-f1e192952714" :answer/id #uuid "606a2a26-1a6c-57ef-b3cd-f1e192952714" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "31.6\\,\\text{lb}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d07ab9ad-d8e6-53a3-916d-ef13c3850d54" :question/id #uuid "d07ab9ad-d8e6-53a3-916d-ef13c3850d54" :question/math-academy-id "q-139802" :question/problem "Suppose the following data are sampled from a population.\n\n$$\n7.3,\\,8.1,\\,6.9,\\,7.6,\\,8.5\n$$\n\nCalculate the value of the statistic $\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}$ for this particular sample." :question/worked-solution "Suppose ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sequence of random variables representing a random sample of size $n$ drawn from a population. A statistic is a random variable expressed as a function of ${X}_{i}.$\n\nStatistics cannot involve unknown population parameters.\n\nNote the following notation:\n\n- ${X}_{i}$ denotes the random variable representing the $i$th observation in a random sample, and\n\n- ${x}_{i}$ is the value of ${X}_{i}$ in a specific sample.\n\nFor the given sample, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{5}{x}_{i} & =\\frac{1}{5}(7.3+8.1+6.9+7.6+8.5) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(38.4) \\\\  & =7.68.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of our statistic for this particular sample is $7.68.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-bd9a0211-1803-541f-9d71-227b97979d9f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-bd9a0211-1803-541f-9d71-227b97979d9f" :answer-field/id #uuid "bd9a0211-1803-541f-9d71-227b97979d9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a9620a00-1aab-52d8-ad63-8a8916da3119" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4dd7ab18-c424-587e-b94f-4966d49cd86c" "answer-8dec3a1d-9535-5c8f-9c8f-05ed89cdf98a" "answer-a9620a00-1aab-52d8-ad63-8a8916da3119" "answer-32a012c8-5672-50ff-9832-8858dc764753" "answer-1f42cb21-e60c-5d40-a114-5979a4cb5b1f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4dd7ab18-c424-587e-b94f-4966d49cd86c" :answer/id #uuid "4dd7ab18-c424-587e-b94f-4966d49cd86c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6.92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8dec3a1d-9535-5c8f-9c8f-05ed89cdf98a" :answer/id #uuid "8dec3a1d-9535-5c8f-9c8f-05ed89cdf98a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a9620a00-1aab-52d8-ad63-8a8916da3119" :answer/id #uuid "a9620a00-1aab-52d8-ad63-8a8916da3119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32a012c8-5672-50ff-9832-8858dc764753" :answer/id #uuid "32a012c8-5672-50ff-9832-8858dc764753" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.91" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1f42cb21-e60c-5d40-a114-5979a4cb5b1f" :answer/id #uuid "1f42cb21-e60c-5d40-a114-5979a4cb5b1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8.21" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]}]
